<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edict of Worms</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Edict of Worms was a decree issued by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> on 25 May 1521, at the close of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-worms">Diet of Worms</a>, declaring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> an outlaw and a heretic. It ordered his arrest, banned the reading and possession of his writings, and forbade anyone to shelter him. Protected by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-elector-of-saxony">Frederick the Wise</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and other princes, Luther was never arrested, and the edict proved impossible to enforce in the German lands where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> took hold.</p></div>
